###############################################
#        WHO READS THIS FILE, AND HOW
###############################################
# Copy to `.env` at the repo root, then `make preflight` (`--fill` asks for
# what is missing). Three things read it:
#
#   docker compose  interpolates every ${...} in the compose files from it
#             (the "docker compose" section at the end), so a required one
#             missing stops every service, not only the one that uses it.
#
#   prod      the file_host container (infra/compose/file_host.yml), through
#             `env_file`. The container then SETS some variables itself, and
#             those win over this file inside it: DATABASE_URL, NATS_URL,
#             REDIS_URL, RUST_LOG (its default), TOKIO_WORKER_THREADS. It
#             always listens on 3000 (published on 127.0.0.1:3000 only; the
#             LAN reaches it through the host's Caddy, file-host.home).
#             orchestrator reads only what infra/compose/orchestrator.yml's
#             `environment:` gives it; a line here reaches it only through
#             a ${...} there.
#
#   make dev  file_host from source (`cargo run`), beside the container. It
#             loads this same file (dotenvy), but anything already in the
#             environment wins - so `FOO=bar make dev` overrides one value
#             for one run. The container's own values above do NOT apply,
#             so here DATABASE_URL and NATS_URL are this file's. It takes
#             the next free port from 3000 (FILE_HOST_PORT_FALLBACK).
#
# Each variable below is listed once, under the first binary that reads it,
# with its help and its default; `<binary> --help` says the same. Every line
# is commented out and shows the default: uncomment one to set it. A copy of
# this file sets nothing, so `make preflight` names each required variable
# until it is set. Unset and empty differ: `NAME=""` is set, to nothing.
#
# HOST-SPECIFIC: values marked so are right only on the nixos.local dev host
# (its domain, its /mnt/storage paths, this checkout's location). Any other
# host - a VPS, say - must set every one of them:
#     grep -n HOST-SPECIFIC example.env
# file_host also warns at startup about each such default it is running on.
# See README.md, "Host-specific values", and #406.
#
# SHARED STATE, READ BEFORE `make dev`: with DATABASE_URL pointed at the
# directory the container mounts, a dev run opens the container's live
# SQLite file, and with NUDGE_ENABLED="true" and the VAPID keys set, runs a
# second nudge waker beside the container's - so a learner can be notified
# twice. For a dev run with its own state:
#     DATABASE_URL="sqlite://$PWD/dev.db" NUDGE_ENABLED="false" make dev
# (migrate dev.db first: see README.md, "Development").
